## 5. Understand the FIM Configuration

The Wazuh agent configuration is commonly stored at:

```text
/var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf
```

Inspect the file:

```bash
sudo less /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf
```

Look for a section similar to:

```xml
<syscheck>
  ...
</syscheck>
```

The `syscheck` section controls File Integrity Monitoring settings, including which paths are monitored and how often periodic checks occur.

**Do not replace the entire configuration file.** Preserve existing settings and back up the file before making any changes.

