## 8. Configure Wazuh to Monitor the Test Directory

This step is optional if you already have FIM enabled for the directory.

First back up the agent configuration:

```bash
sudo cp /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf \
/var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf.bak
```

Open the configuration:

```bash
sudo nano /var/ossec/etc/ossec.conf
```

Inside the existing `<syscheck>` section, add the following entry if it is not already present:

```xml
<directories check_all="yes">/home/YOUR_USERNAME/fim-lab</directories>
```

Replace `YOUR_USERNAME` with your actual Linux username.

For example, if your username is `ubuntu`, use:

```xml
<directories check_all="yes">/home/ubuntu/fim-lab</directories>
```

Keep the entry inside the existing `<syscheck>` section. Do not add a second outer `<syscheck>` block without checking the existing configuration.

The `check_all` setting enables monitoring of supported file attributes. Verify the behavior against the Wazuh version and configuration you are using.

Save the file and exit the editor.

